*---------------------------------------------------------- 948 simple_output_61
* SCRIP keeps label-scanning text physically AFTER a valid END statement; SPITBOL stops at END.
* Two identical trailing lines here trigger a spurious "duplicate label" parse error in scrip.
* Root cause behind csnobol4_suite/sudoku.sno, where the puzzle-grid text after END repeats a
* row verbatim.  sbl -bf prints "hi" cleanly (rc=0); scrip refuses to compile at all.
	OUTPUT = 'hi'
END
data line
data line
*---------------------------------------------------------- 949 simple_output_92
*  f21: OUTPUT() association to a FILE-DESCRIPTOR spec, '[-fn]' with no filename.
*  Routed by hq_P 2026-08-28: every write to the associated variable was silently discarded --
*  rc=0, ordinary output correct, the associated write simply gone. -f1 (not -f2) is the witness
*  here because the board compares stdout; the defect was never fd2-specific, -f1 was dropped too.
        OUTPUT(.E1, 3, '[-f1]')
        E1 = 'via-fd1'
        OUTPUT = 'done'
END
