*  rtx_func_11_include.sno -- WITNESS for RTX-FUNC-11.
*  Two-sided: this (-INCLUDE) arm SEGVs under SCRIP mode 3 and mode 4;
*  the byte-identical inline arm (rtx_func_11_inline.sno) is correct.
*  SPITBOL oracle runs BOTH arms correctly -- .ref is the oracle output.
-INCLUDE 'rtx_func_11_inc.sno'
    OUTPUT = 'i=' i
    OUTPUT = 'B=' B
    OUTPUT = 'DONE'
END
*---------------------------------------------------------- 954 simple_output_85
* CONTROL, GREEN TODAY.  Alternative evaluation `( e1, e2 )` -- manual v3.7 p.99
* "Alternative Evaluation" + Appendix note 3 -- when the FIRST element SUCCEEDS.
* SCRIP lowers TT_VLIST as e1 alone, so this half has always been right; it is here
* so that the two RED siblings cannot be mistaken for "the construct is unparsed".
        q       =
        OUTPUT  = 'first-ok  [' (IDENT(q) 0, 7) ']'
        OUTPUT  = 'lit       [' (1, 2) ']'
        OUTPUT  = 'cat       [' ('p' 'q', 'r') ']'
END
