*-------------------------------------------- 1487 arb_pos_rpos_replace_branch_6
*  ⭐ CURED s189 (row atp-cursor-assign-retry).  Was checked in RED at s188 under law 0d.
*  The stored pattern `E = ARB @v` matched through the PAT$n blob emitted `PAT$0_β: jmp PAT$0_ω`
*  and conceded at the @ node, never reaching the ARB, while the INLINE twin (ptw_min_atp_inline_ctl)
*  was green.  CAUSE: IR_MATCH_ATP was absent from zdp_seam_tier's switch entirely, so it fell to
*  `default: return 0` and resume_carrier_ok refused it -- a silent refusal nobody decided on.
*  CURE: one case label, tier 2, under its own SCRIP_ATP_SEAMTIER knob (ATP owns bb_match_atp.cpp,
*  a different box family from bb_match_capture, so it gets its own independently-revertable knob).
*  MEASURED: the inline β is `add rsp, 16; jmp n4_match_arb_β` -- self-undo fail-through jumping
*  LEFTWARD, the tier-2 definition verbatim.  MANUAL GROUND, v3.7 p.66, a worked example not a rule:
*  `'DOUBT' ? @OUTPUT 'B'` prints 0,1,2,3 -- @ re-fires on EVERY retry and its assignment stands
*  even when the match ultimately fails, so like $ (p.87) there is no undo to get wrong.
          E = ARB @v
          'a+aa' POS(0) E RPOS(0)               :S(OK)F(NO)
OK        OUTPUT = 'match' v                    :(END)
NO        OUTPUT = 'nomatch'
END
*-------------------------------------- 1488 fence_span_capture_replace_branch_1
*	FZ-2: what the cut may release is the CONTIGUOUS backtrack-only frontier and nothing under it.
*	A: capture closed BEFORE the fence -- the SPAN cell above the SAVE is dead and bills 16; the
*	   SAVE cursor under it is live and bounds the walk (it is excluded BY NAME, never released).
*	B: bare leaf before the fence, capture after it -- the leaf is releasable, bills 16.
*	C: two fences -- each bills only the leaf carved since the previous cut; a FENCE0 stops the walk.
*	D: the capture GROUP wraps the fence, so its COND reads the SAVE cursor back AFTER the cut --
*	   the release must not touch it.
	S = 'aaabbbccc'
	S ? SPAN('a') . X FENCE SPAN('b') . Y	:F(BAD)
	OUTPUT = 'A=' X '/' Y
	S ? SPAN('a') FENCE SPAN('b') . Z	:F(BAD)
	OUTPUT = 'B=' Z
	S ? SPAN('a') . P FENCE SPAN('b') FENCE SPAN('c') . Q	:F(BAD)
	OUTPUT = 'C=' P '/' Q
	S ? (SPAN('a') FENCE SPAN('b')) . W	:F(BAD)
	OUTPUT = 'D=' W	:(END)
BAD	OUTPUT = 'UNEXPECTED-FAIL'
END
*----------------------------- 1489 user_function_defer_capture_replace_branch_1
* AB-0 witness: function called MID-MATCH via deferred *F() -- activation opens while
* the match registers are live; the frame must save/restore them (Sigma/cursor).
	DEFINE('MK()')			:(MK_END)
MK	CNT = CNT + 1
	MK = 'B'			:(RETURN)
MK_END
	CNT = 0
	P = 'A' *MK() 'C'
	'ABC' ? P			:S(M1)F(M2)
M1	OUTPUT = 'match OK cnt=' CNT	:(M3)
M2	OUTPUT = 'no match cnt=' CNT
M3	OUTPUT = 'subject intact test'
	S = 'xABCx'
	S ? 'A' *MK() 'C' . R		:S(M4)F(M5)
M4	OUTPUT = 'second OK R=' R ' cnt=' CNT	:(M6)
M5	OUTPUT = 'second FAIL cnt=' CNT
M6
END
