*------------------------------------------------ 1543 arbno_break_len_replace_2
*  RED, CHECKED IN RED (law 0d).  ***AN ARBNO PRECEDED BY ANOTHER ELEMENT NEVER RETRIES,
*  AND THE STATEMENT RUNS AWAY.***  Reduced from corpus/programs/csnobol4-suite/breakx's
*  second statement (BREAK(' ') ARBNO(LEN(1) BREAK(' '))).  BREAKX itself is CURED (s192,
*  rty-fail-inline-retry) -- this is a DIFFERENT, still-open defect: ARBNO's own retry
*  wiring, when ARBNO is NOT the leftmost element of its (...)$ group.  The oracle prints
*  each extension t/th/thi/this/... up to the literal; SCRIP prints "this" forever.
*  ⛔ CAPTURE STDOUT WITH A HARD timeout WHEN RUNNING THIS -- SCRIP DOES NOT TERMINATE.
	&ANCHOR = 1
	subj = "this is a test ."
	subj (BREAK(' ') ARBNO(LEN(1))) $ OUTPUT '.'
END
*------------------------------------------ 1544 fence_pos_rpos_replace_branch_1
*  CONTROL FOR CLASS (a), AND A THIRD CLASS IN ITS OWN RIGHT -- NO FENCE ANYWHERE.  body_root IS
*  published (no RESUME-NIL line) and the blob is STILL red: an ALT top whose arm is itself a concat
*  ending in an alternation publishes the arm's first node as the resume carrier, so an external
*  beta re-enters an exhausted inner alternation and concedes instead of walking out to the ALT.
*  Not the fence rung; own row.  The barer twin ( 'a' | 'aa' ) is green, which is what makes this
*  a carrier-SELECTION defect and not a missing-carrier one.
          P = ( 'a' ('b' | epsilon) | 'aa' )
          'aa' POS(0) *P RPOS(0)                :S(OK)F(NO)
OK        OUTPUT = 'match'                      :(END)
NO        OUTPUT = 'nomatch'
END
*------------------------------------------ 1545 fence_pos_rpos_replace_branch_2
*  CLASS (a) IN BEAUTY'S OWN SHAPE -- beauty's Real (line 55) and White (line 70) are both an ALT
*  TOP with a FENCE nested inside an arm: ( X FENCE(..) .. | Y ).  Same signature as the witness
*  above (pfenced=1 right_sealed=0 rn=0), but SCRIP_FENCE_IGNORE=1 DOES NOT CURE IT -- publishing
*  the first-allocated body node as the carrier lands INSIDE arm 1, not on the ALT, so the blob
*  still cannot offer arm 2.  The fence-free control ptw_min_alttop_nofence_ctl proves that second
*  wall exists with no fence anywhere.
          P = ( 'a' FENCE(epsilon) | 'aa' )
          'aa' POS(0) *P RPOS(0)                :S(OK)F(NO)
OK        OUTPUT = 'match'                      :(END)
NO        OUTPUT = 'nomatch'
END
